<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qutlugh Khwaja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1299</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qutlugh Khwaja was a Chagataid prince, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duwa">Duwa</a>, who commanded the Chagatai forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and led raids into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. In 1299 he led a large army to Kili on the outskirts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a> met him in battle. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> withdrew, and Qutlugh Khwaja died of wounds received in the fighting.</p></div>
